-- title:
--   The number of full output records is at most the squared magnitude
-- statement:
--   For a natural input size $n$, put $m=\operatorname{log2}(n)$, $h=\lfloor\lfloor\sqrt[3]{m}\rfloor/2\rfloor$, $J=20\lfloor m/(200h)\rfloor$, and $M=2^{2048(m+1)}$. Here $\operatorname{log2}(0)=0$ and natural division by zero is zero.
--   Let $T$ be the local schedule length and $Q=\binom{512h}{2h}$ the number of output subsets in one block. The full global output-record count satisfies
--   $$(TQ)^J\le M^2.$$
--   Each record retains both its schedule occurrence and its output subset at every block.
--
--   This supplies a size-only bound for the right-hand physical index of a wanted pair.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/c0ldzy17/three-sum-lean/blob/2b639655e07421b9ac743de9090459bab473a7c0/Submission/ThreeSum/SharedReportingBankResourceBoundsWantedIndices.lean#L44-L56

